<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">General Company of Grão-Pará and Maranhão</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1755">1755</a>–<a href="/years/1778">1778</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Companhia Geral do Grão-Pará e Maranhão</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The General Company of Grão-Pará and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maranhao">Maranhão</a> was a Portuguese chartered trading company founded in 1755 by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marquis-of-pombal">Marquis of Pombal</a>, with a monopoly of trade and shipping between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> and northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>. It shipped tens of thousands of enslaved Africans, mainly from Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a>, to the region, and promoted the export of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cacao">cacao</a>. Its privileges were abolished in 1778 after Pombal's fall.</p></div>
